{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-blowup-cohomological-address","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:blowup-cohomological-address","kind":"remark","title":"Cohomological address of an NS counter-example","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-blowup-yekutieli","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-local-cohomology-group"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-blowup-yekutieli","tags":["blowup","cohomology","singular-set","hausdorff-dimension"],"text":"blowup-cohomological-address.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:blowup-cohomological-address\"></a><p><strong>Location of a counter-example: the cohomological address.</strong>\nA counter-example to NS regularity is a quintuple:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  (v_0, T^*, \\Sigma, n^*, \\kappa_{n^*})</code></pre>\n<p>consisting of:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Initial data</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_0 \\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb{R}^3)</code>, divergence-free, finite energy.</li>\n<li><strong>Blowup time</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T^* &#x3C; \\infty</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Singular set</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Sigma \\subset \\mathbb{R}^3</code> — the spatial locus where regularity fails.</li>\n<li><strong>Obstruction level</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n^* \\in \\mathbb{N}</code> — the brane tower level where lifting fails.</li>\n<li><strong>Obstruction class</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\kappa_{n^*} \\in H^2(\\Sigma, \\mathcal{B})</code> — the nonzero cohomology class preventing the lift.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Sobolev embedding relates the Hausdorff dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_H(\\Sigma)</code> and the obstruction level <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n^*</code>:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_H(\\Sigma)</code></th>\n<th>Blowup geometry</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n^*</code></th>\n<th>Singular <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H^s</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code></td>\n<td>Point</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\geq 3</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s^* &#x3C; 3/2</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td>Filament</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\geq 2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s^* &#x3C; 2</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code></td>\n<td>Sheet</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\geq 1</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">s^* &#x3C; 5/2</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/blowup-cohomological-address.md","heading":"Remark","number":"5.5.2"}
